{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quartz oscillator timekeeping quartz oscillator timekeeping","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md","fileName":"Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:56\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Pre-Satellite Navigation Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Pre-Satellite Navigation Systems","gps.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"quartz oscillator timekeeping quartz oscillator timekeeping","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md","fileName":"Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping","heading":"Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A quartz oscillator uses the crystal's piezoelectric resonance as a stable frequency reference. Its rapid, regular vibration permits more precise portable timekeeping than a mechanical balance wheel, which made accurate radio navigation and early satellite transmitters practical. Quartz is not perfectly invariant: temperature, contamination, shock, and aging can shift its frequency, so demanding systems monitor or correct its drift against a better standard.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Pre-Satellite Navigation Systems","gps.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Quartz Oscillator Timekeeping